=== [REVIEWER_THOUGHT] ===
The code is properly decoupled. The core business logic resides in `src/converter.py` (which is read-only and contains pure mathematical functions), while `src/app.py` handles the GUI orchestration. The `_perform_conversion` method in `ConverterApp` acts as a controller that bridges the UI (getting input from `self.input_entry`) and the logic (calling `conversion_func`), but the actual math is isolated in pure functions. This makes the logic easily testable without needing a GUI environment.

